# Valgrind suppressions for the native-checks valgrind leg.
#
# arrow and data.table are Suggests used by the tests and examples. Each
# starts worker threads it keeps for the life of the process: arrow's
# thread pool when its shared object loads, and data.table's OpenMP pool
# through libgomp. Each thread's thread-local storage is still referenced
# only by an interior pointer when R exits, which valgrind calls "possibly
# lost". The matches are limited to that kind of leak and to stacks that
# pass through those libraries, so a leak in decimal's own code is still
# reported.
{
   arrow-thread-pool-tls
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: possible
   ...
   obj:*/arrow/libs/arrow.so
   ...
}

{
   data-table-openmp-pool-tls
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: possible
   ...
   obj:*/libgomp.so*
   ...
   obj:*/data.table/libs/data_table.so
   ...
}
